[2] Tournament Analysis over exponent schedules
  observable: lower coefficient slope wins; tie by lower ghost support
  score histogram: {0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1, 4: 1, 5: 1, 6: 1}
  directed 3-cycles: 0
  order: eta_all -> random_prime_pm -> liouville -> prime_only -> mobius -> random_pm -> squarefree_only

[3] Reading
  b_m are Witt/product coordinates; G(n)=sum_{d|n} d b_d are ghost
  coordinates.  Eta_all has dense ghost sigma_1 but sparse coefficients.
  Prime_only has sparse exponents but dense ghost on multiples of primes.
  Mobius/Liouville convert multiplicative signs into ordinary product
  gates; coefficient growth and ghost support separate cleanly.
